# Environment and secrets
#
# .env carries the live Databricks account ID, workspace IDs, the service
# principal application ID and its OAuth secret. The committed documents under
# docs/ write those as ${PLACEHOLDER} and resolve them from .env, so a fresh
# clone is missing identifiers, never a conclusion. .env.example is the
# committed template and is re-included below.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.env

# Credentials this repository must never carry: the service principal OAuth
# secret, a Databricks personal access token, and the Vocareum API token.
*.pat
*.pem
*.key
databricks.cfg
.databrickscfg
vocareum-handoff-*.json
secrets.json
credentials.json

# Private working notes and drafted requests to Vocareum support.
support/
*.local.md

# Audit logs and run transcripts. Both record the Databricks account ID, the
# workspace URL, and the operator's identity.
*.log
logs/
probe-run-*.json

